---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site';

const description =
  'About Dastan Aitzhanov: a career across cloud, data, AI, investing, and the questions connecting them.';
---

<Base title="About" description={description}>
  <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      I have always had two tracks running at the same time: building systems and allocating
      capital. They increasingly look like the same problem from different sides.
    </p>
    <p>
      On the technical side, my work has moved through cloud infrastructure, data platforms,
      machine learning, and AI. I worked at Amazon Web Services and Databricks. The problems that
      held my attention were rarely just about the technology itself. They were about the boundary
      between architecture and actual use: what information a system needs, where it should run,
      what can fail, and what a person has to trust before putting it into ordinary work.
    </p>
    <p>
      In parallel, I have spent about a decade investing personal and family capital. Hotels and
      multifamily real estate have been a meaningful part of that experience, alongside public
      equities, technology, private investments, and other alternatives. Investing changes what
      looks important. A model can be elegant and still miss the operating fact that decides the
      outcome.
    </p>
    <p>
      The overlap is what interests me now. I am thinking about AI systems that are more persistent,
      more personal, and more capable of acting: how they use context, when work should stay local,
      how models and tools should be routed, where deterministic systems should take over, and how
      people remain accountable when software can execute.
    </p>
    <p>
      I am equally interested in what those systems change about businesses themselves: knowledge
      work, organizational design, operating leverage, capital allocation, and ownership. This site
      is where I try to turn those questions into writing, small experiments, and ideas that are
      specific enough to be wrong.
    </p>
    <p>I live in Texas.</p>
    <p>
      Email is the simplest way to reach me:
      <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      You can also find me on <a href={site.linkedin} rel="me">LinkedIn</a> and
      <a href={site.github} rel="me">GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
